Z||000000||Monkeyman||11-13-2001||09:17 AM||||My windshield washer pump refuses to work.  It's been this way ever since I've owned the car (last summer).  I tried replacing the pump with a brand new one, but no luck.  It's just not getting power.  I replaced the wiper motor circuit board.  Again, no luck (although that did seem to cure my phantom wipers  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ).  The previous owner claimed to have replaced the steering column.  <P>What possibilities have I overlooked?  I'm starting to get a little aggrevated.  Someone help me, please.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PontiacAPE.jpg">    <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||8
Z||000001||Kasdan||11-13-2001||09:32 AM||||Ive heard something about dropping the pump on the ground, something about a gear, i dunno, probably someone just joking around, i dunno, lol.<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kassig2.gif">                  <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering, Rebuilt 2.8<BR>http://www.geocities.com/mtyler14/index.html||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||11-13-2001||10:17 AM||||Fluid in the line frozen?  Mine is  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Seriously, just trace the wire to find why no power.  You can check the pump easy enough. I'd just run a new circuit to a separate button.<P>PS I have that phantom wiper thing, too.<BR>Gary||||reg||6
Z||000003||stsmithgt||11-13-2001||10:40 AM||||I'd take a second look at the switch in the column.  If it's not the switch itself, possibly one of the connections may need some attention.  Did <B>he</B> replace the switch or a professional?(not that that makes much difference. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)  It doesn't take much to mess one of those switches up and it looks like a project someone may want to shortcut somehow being in the column.  Check for jerry rigs. <BR>plink<BR>plink<BR> 2¢<P>------------------<BR>My work of art 4..s..money. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/4money.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||11-13-2001||02:51 PM||||He said that <B>he</B> replaced the entire column due to the phantom wiper problem (which, of course, wasn't fixed).  I don't think the w/w pump worked either before nor after the column swap.  How do I replace the column switch?||||reg||1
Z||000005||286SE'S||11-13-2001||03:32 PM||||My washers have not worked in years. The delay function was dead and it "parked" anywhere it wanted to on the glass. Since it was going to be raining this week I finally got around to replacing the whole motor last Sunday.<BR>Everything works perfectly now and to my surprize so does the washer!<BR>The wash circuit goes through the motor somehow. I had replaced the circuit board and it made no difference.<BR>I tested it before replacing  by just plugging in the connector to the new motor but you will need a ground wire to the car frame from the motor, look for a strap to one of the mounting screws.<BR>Terry||||reg||1
